(7215966, 1111523, 97225, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how you did this. I don''t even know exactly what I''m looking at, but it is absolutely fascinating and beautiful as well. Top pick. 10</td>', 'I don''t know how you did this. I don''t even know exactly what I''m looking at, but it is absolutely fascinating and beautiful as well. Top pick. 10', '2014-05-12 21:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216060, 1111890, 101668, '<td valign="top">great take on the challenge</td>', 'great take on the challenge', '2014-05-13 09:20:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216134, 1111729, 138253, '<td valign="top">Symmetrical (mostly) but feels somewhat flat. It feels like you''re on a slight angle and have cropped this to get the symmetry in the image, mostly this is due to the bannister on screen-left being three-dimensional while the one on the right seems flatly two-dimensional.<br/>increas in contrast might help this pop out a bit more, and it seems that you missed out on a chance at some wonderful natural lighting.<br/>6 from me.</td>', 'Symmetrical (mostly) but feels somewhat flat. It feels like you''re on a slight angle and have cropped this to get the symmetry in the image, mostly this is due to the bannister on screen-left being three-dimensional while the one on the right seems flatly two-dimensional.increas in contrast might help this pop out a bit more, and it seems that you missed out on a chance at some wonderful natural lighting.6 from me.', '2014-05-13 13:48:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216136, 1111969, 138253, '<td valign="top">this would honestly feel a lot more symmetrical to me if your hands were not mucking about in the picture throwing a tilt on my perspective. you have introduced a second variable that you have tried to make symmetrical, and mostly succeeded in, but they are not symmetrically placed around the skull and it comes off feeling disjointed.<br/>The primary subject is definitely interesting enough to stand on its own and i feel you are going to lose points on this for the above stated reasons.<br/>a 6 from me, probably would''ve been an 8 or 9 without the hands</td>', 'this would honestly feel a lot more symmetrical to me if your hands were not mucking about in the picture throwing a tilt on my perspective. you have introduced a second variable that you have tried to make symmetrical, and mostly succeeded in, but they are not symmetrically placed around the skull and it comes off feeling disjointed.The primary subject is definitely interesting enough to stand on its own and i feel you are going to lose points on this for the above stated reasons.a 6 from me, probably would''ve been an 8 or 9 without the hands', '2014-05-13 13:51:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216137, 1111528, 138253, '<td valign="top">I''m quite enjoying this entry and it looks very familiar (though that could be just because of the haze making the hill look quite generic). <br/>The layers of symmetry work well here, and though not identical, they are still symmetrical and pleasing to the eye.<br/>I hope this does well, but sadly I feel this will be missed by many.<br/>a 9 from me.</td>', 'I''m quite enjoying this entry and it looks very familiar (though that could be just because of the haze making the hill look quite generic). The layers of symmetry work well here, and though not identical, they are still symmetrical and pleasing to the eye.I hope this does well, but sadly I feel this will be missed by many.a 9 from me.', '2014-05-13 13:53:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216138, 1111947, 138253, '<td valign="top">Love the figures in this chess set and the setup of the players on the board.<br/>Personally I may have gone for a slightly tighter crop, but then again i''m not exactly known for my dpc-lauded images.<br/>7 from me</td>', 'Love the figures in this chess set and the setup of the players on the board.Personally I may have gone for a slightly tighter crop, but then again i''m not exactly known for my dpc-lauded images.7 from me', '2014-05-13 13:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216141, 1112048, 138253, '<td valign="top">Well this certainly stands out from the pack, and that is not a bad thing.<br/>I would truly love to see the full image without the cropped top/bottom for the rings to be complete, but the forced perspective into the inner ring will certainly throw people off enough to demand more attention (and isn''t that what art is about? Standing up and screaming Look at Me, Over Here, Pay Attention!!).<br/>I love the title and the sense of imagination this creates: what is forming? how large or small are we seeing here? is this the cause of great wonder or great worry? <br/>I love this image and hope to see it ending high.<br/>9</td>', 'Well this certainly stands out from the pack, and that is not a bad thing.I would truly love to see the full image without the cropped top/bottom for the rings to be complete, but the forced perspective into the inner ring will certainly throw people off enough to demand more attention (and isn''t that what art is about? Standing up and screaming Look at Me, Over Here, Pay Attention!!).I love the title and the sense of imagination this creates: what is forming? how large or small are we seeing here? is this the cause of great wonder or great worry? I love this image and hope to see it ending high.9', '2014-05-13 14:01:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(7216143, 1111523, 138253, '<td valign="top">this has me truly perplexed how you created this eye-catching piece of art. it looks like there are multiple image captures here, perhaps a long exposure with something covering the lens between positionings.<br/>I want to come back to this later and spend some more time trying to unravel it''s mystery.</td>', 'this has me truly perplexed how you created this eye-catching piece of art. it looks like there are multiple image captures here, perhaps a long exposure with something covering the lens between positionings.I want to come back to this later and spend some more time trying to unravel it''s mystery.', '2014-05-13 14:03:58.000000', NULL, 1),
